            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac nuclear imaging is recognized as a relatively safe and reliable noninvasive technique. Various parameters of cardiac function can be analyzed during rest and exercise, thus making it an important adjunct in the diagnosis and management of coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
